From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:45:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 153/342] meson_uart: the ODROID-C2 header's UART A as
 /dev/ports/header

A serial port on header pins 8 (TX) and 10 (RX), 3.3 V, for BSerialPort
("header") and termios programs. The device tree has the UART disabled
and its pins are GPIO until the port is opened: opening claims them in
meson_header (B_BUSY while a program has one) and selects UART A;
closing lets the bytes written go out, then gives them back.

Programs get the slave side of a tty pair, as with a pty, so termios
works as on a terminal (VMIN and VTIME included); the driver is the
master side, a thread passing received bytes in and one sending what
comes out, into the 128-byte FIFO, woken when it is below half full.
Two-wire: no RTS/CTS on the header. The baud clock is 8 MHz divided by
a 23-bit divider: 500k to 4M exact, 9600 to 230400 within 0.8 %. A
break inverts TX. Measured on the ODROID-C2 from pin 8: frames in 8N1,
8E1 and 7O2, and speeds from 9600 to 4000000 within 0.02 % without gaps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
